#!/bin/bash

# tam-setup-security-fingerprint — enrol a fingerprint and use it for sudo and
# polkit.
#
# Ported from Omarchy 4.0.4 (omarchy-setup-security-fingerprint) for plan 18
# R4.15g. Changed: the clamshell gate in the PAM stacks is a shell test of the
# lid state run by /usr/bin/sh, not a packaged helper, so it outlives the
# package that provided one. No lock-screen PAM file is written: hyprlock
# (plan 18 R4.16) talks to fprintd itself. The driver is Arch's libfprint,
# installed with fprintd through tam-pkg-add, instead of libfprint-git from a
# repository Tamlinux is leaving.
#
